<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">FAQs</p>
      <h2>Questions Melbourne homeowners ask us</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq" style="max-width:760px">
      <details open><summary>How do I get started with a solar installation?</summary><p>Use the 60-second quote form above, or call us. We'll ask about your bills, roof and switchboard, then design a system and give you a fixed written quote — no obligation, no door-knockers.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do solar panels work on cloudy days?</summary><p>Yes — output drops but doesn't stop. A well-sized system is designed around your annual usage, and pairing it with a battery lets you ride through low-generation days.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Am I eligible for Victorian solar rebates?</summary><p>Most owner-occupied homes under the income and property-value thresholds qualify for Solar Victoria rebates. As a Solar Victoria Authorised Retailer we handle the paperwork and confirm your eligibility before you commit.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you install a battery if my solar was installed by someone else?</summary><p>Absolutely — battery retrofits are one of our core services. We assess your existing inverter and switchboard, then recommend a compatible battery with backup supply.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What warranty do I get?</summary><p>A 5-year installation workmanship warranty from us, on top of the manufacturer warranties on panels (typically 25 years performance), inverters and batteries (typically 10 years).</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
